text:
{
"opening": "This release introduces significant enhancements to date parsing and formatting capabilities, specifically targeting ISO 8601 week dates and microsecond precision. It also expands localization support for human-readable timeframes across several European and Asian locales while consolidating existing German-based locale implementations.",
"requirements": [
{
"id": "m09",
"text": "The DateTimeParser must accept strings formatted as ISO 8601 week dates using the 'W' token, such as '2013-W29-6', and correctly resolve them to their corresponding calendar dates. The DateTimeFormatter must support the 'W' token in format strings to output dates in the ISO 8601 week date format, raising a ParserMatchError if the input string does not conform to the expected pattern."
},
{
"id": "m12",
"text": "The DateTimeFormatter must support the lowercase 'x' token to format datetime objects as Unix timestamps with millisecond precision (microseconds included) and the uppercase 'X' token for second precision."
},
{
"id": "m13",
"text": "The public functions get_locale and get_locale_by_class_name must remain available and functional, ensuring that locale retrieval mechanisms continue to operate without regression despite internal test infrastructure changes."
},
{
"id": "m14",
"text": "The PolishLocale must provide humanized timeframes with week granularity, returning appropriate localized strings for singular and plural week intervals when calculating relative time differences."
},
{
"id": "m15",
"text": "The GermanBaseLocale, GermanLocale, AustrianLocale, SwissLocale, MacedonianLocale, RomanianLocale, and RomanshLocale classes must consistently handle 'week' and 'weeks' granularity in humanized descriptions, with SwissLocale functionality consolidated into the base German locale handling to ensure predictable behavior for 'de' language codes."
},
{
"id": "m17",
"text": "The ChineseTWLocale must support humanized timeframes with week granularity, providing correct localized translations for singular and plural week intervals in the Traditional Chinese locale."
}
],
"closing": "Please ensure all new formatting tokens and locale updates are verified against the public API contracts to maintain backward compatibility. These changes extend the library's utility for international users and precise timestamp handling."
}
